{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbG6csA7kKrwN3XeRNAR", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The tests use pytest, with two Makefile targets:\n\n```bash\npip install -e .[dev]   # one-time: installs pytest and the app's dependencies\n\nmake test-fast          # pytest -m \"not postgres\" -q  (skips tests marked postgres)\nmake test               # pytest -q                    (full suite, includes postgres tests)\n```\n\n`make test-fast` is the one to use day to day; a saved project note also names it as the usual command. It skips the tests marked `postgres`, so it should work without a database. Use `make test` when you need the full suite, which includes those Postgres tests, so you'll need a database available.\n\nTo run one file or one test, call pytest directly, e.g. `pytest tests/<file>.py -k <name> -q`.\n\nI haven't run either target here, so I can't confirm the suite currently passes."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 626, "cache_read_input_tokens": 18644, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 626}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "318b192b-65a7-417a-aead-7b12d5ec0dbe", "uuid": "4531cc44-1895-4ed0-a054-34bc1c777f39", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T09:13:39.486Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbG6cWKt6azJmZS5Z4UE"}
